# Accepted Trivy findings (issue #156). Every entry gives its reason and expires, so
# the scan fails again on the review date. Never add an entry without a reason.

# AWS-0040 (CRITICAL), EKS public endpoint: the endpoint is public only for the
# operator's /32 (public_access_cidrs), and private access is on. The operator runs
# Terraform, Helm and kubectl from outside the VPC; there is no bastion or VPN.
AWS-0040 exp:2027-03-31

# AWS-0104 (CRITICAL), unrestricted egress from the node security groups: nodes pull
# images from GHCR and reach AWS APIs through the single NAT gateway. Restricting
# egress needs VPC endpoints and a GHCR mirror, which are future work.
AWS-0104 exp:2027-03-31

# AWS-0039 (HIGH), no KMS envelope encryption of Kubernetes Secrets: the cluster only
# lives for a cloud day and its Secrets hold disposable test credentials; a customer
# managed KMS key is future work for a long-lived environment.
AWS-0039 exp:2027-03-31
